<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Galeazzo Ciano</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1903–1944</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Galeazzo Ciano was an Italian Fascist politician, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Benito Mussolini</a>'s son-in-law and foreign minister from 1936 to 1943. His diaries are a major source for Fascist foreign policy. In July 1943 he voted in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-council-qing">Grand Council</a> against Mussolini, who was then deposed; he was later tried by the Italian Social Republic at Verona and shot in January 1944.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/galeazzo-ciano.jpg" alt="Galeazzo Ciano" width="320" height="347" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Galeazzo_Ciano01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
